  "review": [
    "The preceding goal turn changed ten source functions and completed focused native checks; it was progress. This batch starts from their hash-checked successful build and preserves the existing index.",
    "The C622 full report is a discovery snapshot. Fresh setup/debug bounds and actual current bytes are used for this batch; historical rebuilt RVAs are not reused after linking.",
    "Full-report callee-family counts identify exactly two native callers still using the deprecated protection helper, plus Thought Prison using the wrong spell-trigger family. The two remaining old protection calls are in unbuilt recoded_cards.c; that file has no emitted current DWARF ranges and is not rewritten without native caller evidence.",
    "Natural Order was found by comparing same-callee outgoing constant arguments in single-call functions. The native generic_spell mode is 0x8000 at 0x201c3dc; source test initialization and control flow were separately inspected before changing the flag.",
    "The two Graven Dominator calls and Dispossess have equivalent current wrapper behavior for these operands. Restoring their explicitly identified native callees improves source/call-graph fidelity, not gameplay semantics.",
    "Repeated Aura masks group the same event set differently (600/700 versus 700/4700 plus other tests); no macro is rewritten to force a preferred GCC block layout. Moved branches, masked type shifts, Kaya threshold encodings and split helper guards remain unchanged.",
    "Raw historical decompiler exports were used only as reading aids; the native instruction stream, exact COFF callees, current source and fresh debug bounds are authoritative. No unverified Ghidra instance was treated as the release image.",
    "One combined build and focused native caller checks follow. Full comparison and historical recovery replay are deferred.",
    "Focused raw-operand verification caught the Thought Prison type-filter assumption before publication: native sp_ability_trigger uses TYPE_ANY (0xff), alongside controller ANYBODY (2), not TYPE_NONE. The final source preserves both distinct arguments."
  ],
